# Stack

Verified August 2026. Check the lockfile before assuming a version — this file states the target, not what's installed.

## Read the installed docs before writing Next.js code
Next.js ships version-matched documentation inside the project. Before writing or changing anything that touches Next.js APIs — routing, caching, metadata, server actions, config — read the guides in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`.

Major versions of Next.js carry breaking changes. The installed docs are correct for the installed version; your training data is not. When the two disagree, the installed docs win.

If `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md` exists at the repo root, read it first — it may point at additional version-specific guidance.

## Standard
- **Next.js 16.x**, App Router. Turbopack is the default bundler. Dev disk caching landed in 16.1; build disk caching in 16.3. Check the installed version before citing either.
- **React 19+** (required by Next 16)
- **TypeScript strict**. TypeScript 7 as the `next build` typechecker requires Next 16.3+. On 16.2 and below, stay on TypeScript 5.x.
- **Tailwind CSS v4.x** — CSS-first config, see below
- **Zod v4** for validation
- **Vercel** for hosting
- **Postgres via Vercel Marketplace (Neon)**. Vercel Postgres was discontinued and migrated to Neon in December 2024. Never scaffold `@vercel/postgres` for a new project.

Config lives in `next.config.ts`, typed with `NextConfig`.

## Tailwind v4
No `tailwind.config.js`. JS config still loads but is not auto-detected — it requires an explicit `@config` line, so don't create one.

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@theme {
  --breakpoint-sm: 24.5rem;
  --breakpoint-md: 50.5rem;
  --breakpoint-lg: 64rem;
  --breakpoint-xl: 90rem;
  --breakpoint-2xl: 120rem;
  --breakpoint-3xl: 240rem;
}
```

Never emit `@tailwind base/components/utilities` — that is v3 syntax and fails in v4.

Baseline: Safari 16.4+, Chrome 111+, Firefox 128+. v4 depends on `@property` and `color-mix()`.

## Caching
`'use cache'` is the caching primitive. No implicit caching, dynamic by default.

`cacheComponents` and `partialPrefetching` are 16.3+ flags. Do not add either to a project below 16.3 — the key is ignored or errors. On 16.3+, ask before enabling: both change rendering behavior across the whole app.

## HIPAA — only when handling PHI
- AWS or Google Cloud under a signed BAA. Not Vercel.
- Encrypted database (RDS or equivalent), encryption at rest and in transit
- Auth0 Healthcare or AWS Cognito
- 15 minute session timeout
- MFA required
- No PHI in logs, URLs, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, analytics, or error reports
- Audit logging on every PHI read and write

If a project touches PHI, say so before writing any storage or logging code.
